# Capital Accounts — <ENTITY NAME>

**Perpetual roll-forward** — one row set per partner/shareholder per year; never reset. Runs from formation through dissolution.
**Basis reported**: tax-basis capital (K-1 Item L, transactional approach) — **not** §704(b) book capital and **not** holder outside basis. See notes below.
**Generated**: YYYY-MM-DD

> Source of truth: `entities/<slug>/entity.md` for ownership %, entry dates, and entity type. This file tracks the running balance only.
> Scope: partnerships and S-corps. A **disregarded SMLLC's** member capital is not tracked here — it lives in the SMLLC's own COA equity accounts (3060/3070) and must mirror the parent's `1860 Investment` account; see `entities/disregarded.md` § two-tier equity model.

## §704(b) vs. tax-basis — why this file is tax-basis

- **Tax-basis capital** (this file): the transactional-approach capital account required on K-1 Item L since 2020 — starts at cash + property contributed (adjusted basis, not FMV), tracks contributions/distributions/income/loss at tax character. It is **not** the partner's outside basis (§705/§1367): outside basis adds the partner's share of liabilities and other holder-level items, and is reconstructed separately in `reconciliation.md` § 5.
- **§704(b) book capital** (partnerships only): FMV-based capital account for partnership-agreement / substantial-economic-effect purposes. It is **not** a K-1 Item L reporting method — since 2020, Item L is tax-basis only. If the partnership agreement requires §704(b) book capital tracking (e.g., for special allocations, revaluations on admission/withdrawal), maintain it separately — do not conflate with this file.
- Since 2020, partnerships must report tax-basis capital on K-1s regardless of the method used for §704(b) purposes — this file is that tax-basis figure.

